---
description: Checkbox toggles only when the square is clicked
alwaysApply: true
---

# Checkbox click target is the square only

A checkbox MUST toggle only when the operator clicks the checkbox **square** itself.

Do **not** wrap the checkbox and its caption in a `<label>` (or otherwise bind the caption click to the input) so that clicking "NOT", "Use condition", "Active", or any other caption text flips the box.

```html
<!-- BAD — whole row toggles -->
<label class="field-check"><input type="checkbox"> Use condition</label>

<!-- GOOD — only the square toggles -->
<div class="field-check">
  <input type="checkbox" id="automationUseCondition">
  <span>Use condition</span>
</div>
```

Checkboxes MUST align to the **left** unless a layout explicitly asks otherwise. Prefer `.field-check`. Do not put a lone checkbox as a stretched child of a column `.field` (browsers center the square in the full-width control).
